opam-version: "2.0"
synopsis: "Proof library for rocq-linux-process-semantics"
description: """
The Rocq theory LinuxProcessSemantics.Common: lemmas, tactics and a
reflective plan checker for proofs of the equivalence and termination
statements of rocq-linux-process-semantics-core about RISC-V binaries.
Most of it was written by the OSS-Fuzz proof collaborators. The header of
each file says where it came from.
"""
maintainer: "Jason Gross <jason@theorem.dev>"
authors: ["The OSS-Fuzz proof collaborators" "Theorem Labs"]
license: "MIT"
homepage: "https://github.com/theorem-labs/rocq-linux-process-semantics"
bug-reports: "https://github.com/theorem-labs/rocq-linux-process-semantics/issues"
dev-repo: "git+https://github.com/theorem-labs/rocq-linux-process-semantics.git"
